FleetMiner Core: modular drone fleet script (miners, haulers, carriers) over IGC.

SETUP
  1. Load the script into a Programmable Block, then edit its Custom Data.
     Recompile once to write every key with its default value.
       [FleetMiner]
       Role=Miner          ; Miner | Hauler | Carrier
       Channel=FLEETMINER  ; must match across the whole fleet
  2. Drones need: a Remote Control (or tag a controller [FM Ref]) facing the
     drill direction, gyros, thrusters on all six sides, an antenna, and one
     connector (tag [FM Dock] to choose).
  3. Optional on miners:
       [FM Cam]    forward camera: finds the rock face, lets 'setsite' work from range
       [FM Eject]  conveyor sorter + ejector: dumps stone while drilling
       [FM LCD]    LCD or cockpit/console screen: status display
       Timers named with a state tag fire on entering that state:
       [FM Docked] [FM Undocking] [FM Transit] [FM Working] [FM RequestDock]
       [FM Approach] [FM FinalDock] [FM Idle]
  4. The carrier offers every connector tagged [FM Dock] (or all of them) as a dock.
     Drones unload into its cargo containers (only [FM Unload] ones, if any are tagged).
     Give a moving carrier a ship controller so it can report its velocity.
  See docs/MinerDrone.md in the source repo for the full build guide.

DRONE COMMANDS (PB argument)
  setsite    Aim at the rock face and run: records the site (and its plane, with a camera).
  start      Begin the automatic mine -> dock -> unload -> launch cycle.
  return     Back out of the shaft, fly home and dock. The cycle stops once docked.
  stop       Halt in place; dampeners on.
  skip       Abandon the current shaft and move to the next one.
  resetsite  Restart the shaft spiral at shaft 0.
  forget     Forget the home carrier (next dock request is broadcast).

CARRIER COMMANDS
  launch | recall | halt   Broadcast to every drone on the channel.
  reset                    Clear all dock reservations.
